Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21194) Speed up the balanced task assignor
 and register it as a built-in assignor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Gavin Wang (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Gavin Wang created KAFKA-21194:
----------------------------------

             Summary: Speed up the balanced task assignor and register it a=
s a built-in assignor
                 Key: KAFKA-21194
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21194
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: Gavin Wang
            Assignee: Gavin Wang


KAFKA-20998 added \{{BalancedTaskAssignor}}, a one-to-one translation of th=
e classic \{{HighAvailabilityTaskAssignor}} placement, not yet registered a=
s a built-in. Its fix-up loop tests every pair of processes on each pass, s=
o it costs =CE=98(P=C2=B2) per pass even when nothing moves: up to 26x the =
sticky assignor's time in JMH (12.4 ms for 1000 single-member processes).

Plan:
# Index-based implementation and an O(P) early exit for passes that cannot =
move a task. Same assignment.
# Place active tasks with the Sainte-Lagu=C3=AB divisor method (next task t=
o the process with the smallest (2n+1)/c), read from a precomputed period, =
instead of round-robin plus fix-up. Same placement for equal member counts;=
 for unequal ones the same per-member balance and a more even spread of eac=
h subtopology. Separate PR, as it changes placement.
# Register \{{balanced}} in \{{GroupCoordinatorConfig.STREAMS_GROUP_BUILTIN=
_ASSIGNORS}} once KIP-1071 is amended from \{{highly_available}}.

Prototypes: 1 is 6-10x faster, 1+2 is 12-19x, about a quarter of the sticky=
 assignor's time.



