Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21195) Use RE2/J in ClientMetricsConfigs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Chia-Ping Tsai (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21195:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Use RE2/J in ClientMetricsConfigs
                 Key: KAFKA-21195
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21195
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


ClientMetricsConfigs uses java.util.regex to compile the match patterns of client metrics subscriptions. We should switch to RE2/J, which is already used by the broker and guarantees linear time matching.

This is a behavior change. A pattern stored on the server may be valid in java.util.regex but invalid in RE2, so we need to catch the error and log a warning instead of failing after upgrade.



