Lianet Magrans created KAFKA-21198:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Consider improving client-side visibility/logging for=
 rejected Oauth token
                 Key: KAFKA-21198
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21198
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Task
          Components: clients
            Reporter: Lianet Magrans
            Assignee: Evan Zhou


The current los when an issue with the token leads to fail auth does not in=
clude anything to help identify the token, which makes it hard to correlate=
 to the broker-side when a token is rejected.

Current client-side logging on token-related failure seems to be around pri=
ncipal only (debug level) here [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/7aba83=
304c69e151597ecfb4e8a004079cdd1ec8/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/c=
ommon/security/oauthbearer/internals/OAuthBearerRefreshingLogin.java#L106]=
=C2=A0

and nothing is logged where I expect the token failure on the related incid=
ent would land on the client side [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/7ab=
a83304c69e151597ecfb4e8a004079cdd1ec8/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafk=
a/common/security/oauthbearer/internals/OAuthBearerSaslClient.java#L100]=C2=
=A0

This task is to review if logging could be improved (considering from the s=
ecurity pov, what would be helpful and acceptable to log)



--
