Subject: [DISCUSS] KIP-1379: Make server-side rack-aware assignment opt-in
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
From: David Jacot <dajac@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Hi all,

I'd like to discuss a small KIP to make server-side rack-aware
assignment opt-in.

Rack-aware assignment only helps when consumers fetch from followers
and the replicas of a partition do not cover every rack, yet the group
coordinator pays for it for every group today. The KIP adds a broker
configuration, off by default, to enable it for consumer groups.

https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/d6fwGg

Best,
David

