morgando commented on code in PR #920:
URL: https://github.com/apache/kafka-site/pull/920#discussion_r4170189298


##########
content/en/39/operations/kraft.md:
##########
@@ -486,9 +486,8 @@ Enter Migration Mode on the brokers
 <td>
 
 
-
-  * Using `zookeeper-shell.sh`, compare the ZooKeeper controller epoch (`get /controller_epoch`) to the KRaft controller epoch (the `kraft_controller_epoch` field in `get /migration`). If the KRaft epoch is higher, run `set /controller_epoch <value>` (where `<value>` exceeds the KRaft epoch) to ensure the ZooKeeper controller will start with a higher epoch after reverting. 
   * Deprovision the KRaft controller quorum. 
+  * Using `zookeeper-shell.sh`, compare the ZooKeeper controller epoch (`get /controller_epoch`) to the KRaft controller epoch (the `kraft_controller_epoch` field in `get /migration`). If the KRaft epoch is higher, run `set /controller_epoch <value>` (where `<value>` exceeds the KRaft epoch) to ensure the ZooKeeper controller will start with a higher epoch after reverting. 

Review Comment:
   I agree that it is good to mention that the check/update epoch step should be done quickly -- made that change :)
   
   To optimize for minimizing the no-controller window, we could maybe do this:
     1. deprovision kraft quorum. 
     2. delete /controller
     3. compare epochs. if kraft epoch > zk epoch, bump zk epoch and delete /controller to trigger another election.
     4. delete /migration
     5. ...
   
   This seems like essentially what you did to recover from https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20488. It would minimize the no-controller window, at the cost of potentially allowing a low-epoch controller to become active briefly in rare cases, with a documented recovery strategy.



