Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21211) Server-side Streams rack-aware
 assignment configuration can accept tag keys longer than 20 characters,
 while the Kafka Streams client rejects such keys during `StreamsConfig`
 construction.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21211:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Server-side Streams rack-aware assignment configurati=
on can accept tag keys longer than 20 characters, while the Kafka Streams c=
lient rejects such keys during `StreamsConfig` construction.
                 Key: KAFKA-21211
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21211
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


*Description*

Server-side Streams rack-aware assignment configuration can accept tag keys=
 longer than 20 characters, while the Kafka Streams client rejects such key=
s during {{StreamsConfig}} construction.

The inconsistency affects both configuration paths:
 * Broker default: {{group.streams.rack.aware.assignment.tags}}
 * Group override: {{streams.rack.aware.assignment.tags}}

For example, the server-side configuration accepts the following 22-charact=
er tag key:

=C2=A0

{{streams.rack.aware.assignment.tags=3Davailability_zone_name}}

However, a Streams client cannot supply the corresponding tag:
 * group.protocol=3Dstreams
 * client.tag.availability_zone_name=3Daz-a

{{StreamsConfig}} throws a {{ConfigException}} because the tag key exceeds =
the client-side maximum length of 20 characters.

*Actual behavior*

The server accepts a rack-aware assignment tag key that the official Stream=
s client cannot provide. Adding the corresponding client tag prevents the a=
pplication from starting; omitting it leaves that tag unavailable to the as=
signor.

*Expected behavior*

Server-side rack-aware assignment configuration should be consistent with t=
he tag keys supported by the Streams client. An unsupported key should be r=
ejected when the configuration is supplied, rather than accepted and discov=
ered later during client startup.

*Suggested fix*

Validate tag key lengths during broker bootstrap and Admin API group config=
uration changes. Reject keys longer than 20 characters with a {{ConfigExcep=
tion}} during bootstrap or the corresponding configuration error through th=
e Admin API. (It would be better to consider length of value - 30)

Compatibility with previously stored configurations should be considered, p=
articularly for configuration queries and metadata restoration.



--
