Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21212) Removed `client.rack` configuration
 is not reflected when a Streams static member rejoins
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21212:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Removed `client.rack` configuration is not reflected =
when a Streams static member rejoins
                 Key: KAFKA-21212
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21212
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


*Description*

When a static member using {{group.protocol=3Dstreams}} restarts after remo=
ving its {{client.rack}} configuration, the coordinator retains the previou=
s rack ID.

During static member replacement, the coordinator copies the previous membe=
r=E2=80=99s metadata and then treats {{RackId=3Dnull}} in the joining reque=
st as unchanged. Changing the rack ID to another value works, but removing =
it does not.

*Conditions*
 # Start a Streams application with {{group.instance.id}} and {{{}client.ra=
ck=3Drack-a{}}}.
 # Shut it down gracefully using the default close behavior.
 # Remove the {{client.rack}} configuration.
 # Restart with the same static instance ID before the session timeout expi=
res.

*Expected behavior*

The coordinator should clear the rack ID to reflect the new client configur=
ation. Since the rack has changed, the group epoch should increase and the =
assignment should be recomputed.

For regular heartbeats, {{RackId=3Dnull}} should continue to mean unchanged=
.

*Actual behavior*

The coordinator retains the previous rack ID. Group descriptions and custom=
 assignors therefore receive stale rack information, and rack removal itsel=
f does not trigger assignment recomputation. If another metadata change tri=
ggers recomputation, the stale rack information is still used.



