Hi David,

Thanks for the KIP. This is a nice simplification for the common case
(and share + streams in all cases).

LB1: The compatibility section covers both broker upgrade and
downgrade. Does the same apply to flipping the config?

LB2: The config is broker-wide, while the benefit depends on the
topics and consumers of each group (i.e., fetch-from-follower is in
use, and replicas do not cover all racks). Did you consider making it
a group-level configuration?

LB3: Streams groups get the one-time rebalance on upgrade/downgrade as
well (but not on a config flip). Could the compatibility section point
this out explicitly?

LB4: The javadoc of SubscribedTopicDescriber#racksForPartition() says
it returns the racks of the partition's replicas, and an empty set
only when the topic does not exist. With the config disabled it would
return an empty set for existing topics, which seems to go against
that contract. It's a minor incompatibility, but maybe worth pointing
out that we are changing this contract.

Cheers,
Lucas

