Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21219) Streams group dynamic member close
 can stall with REMAIN\_IN\_GROUP after poll timeout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "sanghyeok An (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21219:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Streams group dynamic member close can stall with REM=
AIN\_IN\_GROUP after poll timeout
                 Key: KAFKA-21219
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21219
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


Closing a Streams group dynamic member with {{REMAIN_IN_GROUP}} can leave t=
he close future incomplete when the poll timer has expired.

{{StreamsMembershipManager.isLeavingGroup()}} returns {{false}} for dynamic=
 members using {{{}REMAIN_IN_GROUP{}}}, even when their state is {{PREPARE_=
LEAVING}} or {{{}LEAVING{}}}. Consequently, {{StreamsGroupHeartbeatRequestM=
anager.poll()}} enters the poll timeout branch despite the member already l=
eaving.

When the member is in {{{}LEAVING{}}}, {{onPollTimerExpired()}} attempts to=
 transition it back to {{{}PREPARE_LEAVING{}}}, throwing:

=C2=A0

{{IllegalStateException: Invalid state transition from LEAVING to PREPARE_L=
EAVING}}

This exception occurs before a heartbeat request is generated and prevents =
the normal path from skipping the leave heartbeat and completing the close =
future.

*Reproduction conditions*
 # Join a Streams group as a dynamic member without configuring {{{}group.i=
nstance.id{}}}.
 # Allow the application poll interval to exceed {{{}max.poll.interval.ms{}=
}}.
 # Before the heartbeat manager processes the poll timeout, process a close=
 request with {{{}REMAIN_IN_GROUP{}}}, transitioning the member to {{{}LEAV=
ING{}}}.
 # On the next heartbeat manager {{{}poll(){}}}, the invalid state transiti=
on exception occurs.

*Expected behavior*

Poll timeout handling should not initiate another leave operation while the=
 member is already preparing to leave or leaving.

For a dynamic member closing with {{{}REMAIN_IN_GROUP{}}}, once the member =
reaches {{{}LEAVING{}}}, the client should skip the leave heartbeat, transi=
tion to {{{}UNSUBSCRIBED{}}}, and complete the close future normally.

While in {{{}PREPARE_LEAVING{}}}, regular heartbeats may continue until the=
 pending callback completes.



