The early return treats "all partitions cold-snapshotted" as "system is qui=
et". But ShareUpdate does not touch createTimestamp or writeTimestamp (see =
merge()), so once every partition has been cold-snapshotted, the timer retu=
rns early on every run until some partition reaches the records threshold. =
Slow-traffic partitions are never flushed, which conflicts with the purpose=
 of the timer.



