sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21229:
------------------------------------

             Summary: AsyncKafkaConsumer passes null offsets to OffsetCommi=
tCallback when an asynchronous commit fails
                 Key: KAFKA-21229
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21229
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


When an asynchronous commit fails in AsyncKafkaConsumer with group.protocol=
=3Dconsumer, the user-provided OffsetCommitCallback receives null instead o=
f the offsets associated with the request.

Both overloads are affected:
{code:java}
consumer.commitAsync(offsets, callback);
consumer.commitAsync(callback);
{code}
Successful commits pass the request offsets correctly.

*Expected behavior*

The callback should receive the offsets and metadata associated with the re=
quest, regardless of whether the commit succeeds or fails. The exception ar=
gument should indicate the failure and its cause.

This is consistent with the documentation for the offsets parameter of Offs=
etCommitCallback.onComplete() and the behavior of the Classic Consumer.

=C2=A0

*Actual behavior and impact*

When an asynchronous commit fails, the callback is invoked as follows:
{code:java}
callback.onComplete(null, exception); {code}
Applications cannot identify or log the offsets associated with the failed =
request using the callback argument. Error-handling code that accesses the =
offsets map may throw a NullPointerException.
{code:java}
consumer.commitAsync((offsets, exception) -> {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 if (exception !=3D null)
{ =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 offsets.forEach((partition, offset) -> =C2=A0=
 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 recordFailure(partition, offset, except=
ion)); =C2=A0 =C2=A0 }
}); {code}
This issue concerns the information provided when reporting a failed commit=
. It does not imply that the issue itself causes commit failures or data lo=
ss.

=C2=A0

*Root cause*

AsyncKafkaConsumer.commitAsync() forwards the committedOffsets value receiv=
ed by the commit future=E2=80=99s whenComplete handler directly to the user=
 callback.

When the future completes exceptionally, committedOffsets` is `null`. The i=
mplementation does not fall back to the explicitly supplied request offsets=
. When offsets are omitted, the offsets calculated in the background are no=
t separately retained for the failure callback either.



