Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21230) Long rebalances can cause OOM errors
 with transactional state stores enabled
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Nicholas Telford (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Nicholas Telford created KAFKA-21230:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: Long rebalances can cause OOM errors with transactional state stores enabled
                 Key: KAFKA-21230
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21230
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 4.4.0
            Reporter: Nicholas Telford


When transactional state stores (KIP-892) are enabled, we loosely bound our transaction buffers using the new {{statestore.uncommitted.max.bytes}}, which is checked in {{StreamThread#maybeCommit()}}.

However, {{TaskManager.commit()}} does not guarantee that it commits: if the thread is currently in the middle of a rebalance, *commits are skipped until it completes*. When this happens, processing continues without a commit until the rebalance has completed.

Long rebalances can therefore cause threads to exceed this limit by a large degree, potentially causing OOM errors (native memory, most likely).



--
