Gergely Harmad=C3=A1s created KAFKA-21237:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: Remove accidental JUnit 4 usage
                 Key: KAFKA-21237
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21237
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Task
            Reporter: Gergely Harmad=C3=A1s
            Assignee: Gergely Harmad=C3=A1s


Currently=C2=A0[StreamsGroupDescribeRequestTest|https://github.com/apache/k=
afka/blob/85387e94364bdf31c6acf06086210d85a9fb0711/core/src/test/scala/unit=
/kafka/server/StreamsGroupDescribeRequestTest.scala#L32] includes accidenta=
l JUnit 4 assert usages. Based on my findings:
 # Historically KAFKA-7339 had the JUnit 4 to JUnit 5 in scope.
 # KAFKA-19153 pulled in a new dependency [Mock OAuth2 Server|https://mvnre=
pository.com/artifact/no.nav.security/mock-oauth2-server/2.3.0] which in tu=
rn depends on JUnit 4
 # KAFKA-19754 probably only used the JUnit 4 asserts by accident since the=
 test library is on the test classpath

As a fix I changed the asserts to the JUnit 5 equivalent and removed JUnit =
4 from the test compile classpath so we can avoid similar accidents in the =
future.

Other things I considered:
 * JUnit 4 can't be excluded from=C2=A0[Mock OAuth2 Server|https://mvnrepos=
itory.com/artifact/no.nav.security/mock-oauth2-server/2.3.0] as it is a run=
time dependency which results in NoClassDefFoundError
 * Tried updating=C2=A0[Mock OAuth2 Server|https://mvnrepository.com/artifa=
ct/no.nav.security/mock-oauth2-server/2.3.0] to latest version but it still=
 pulls in JUnit 4



--
