sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21238:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Mutating nested sets in consumer assignor input can c=
orrupt coordinator target assignment state
                 Key: KAFKA-21238
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21238
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


*Description*

{{MemberSubscriptionAndAssignmentImpl}} retains an {{Assignment}} that refe=
rences the coordinator=E2=80=99s existing target assignment. Although {{Ass=
ignment}} wraps the outer map with {{{}Collections.unmodifiableMap(){}}}, t=
he nested partition sets remain mutable.

If a custom assignor uses the input assignment as a working data structure =
and modifies a nested set, it also modifies the coordinator=E2=80=99s exist=
ing target assignment before returning the assignment result.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

KS also had similar issue https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20846=
 and it had been resolved.

=C2=A0

*Actual Behavior*

A local reproduction of the Consumer path demonstrated the following:
 * The existing target assignment changes from {{{0, 1}}} to {{{1}}} during=
 assignor execution.
 * {{TargetAssignmentBuilder}} considers the existing assignment and the re=
turned result equal, so it does not generate a target assignment change rec=
ord for the member.
 * The reverse index still retains the ownership information for partition =
0.
 * Rolling back to the snapshot does not restore partition 0 in the nested =
set.

This can leave the coordinator=E2=80=99s in-memory state, reverse index, an=
d logged state inconsistent.

*Expected Behavior*

The input assignment provided to the assignor should be immutable and isola=
ted from coordinator state. Attempts to modify nested partition sets should=
 be rejected without affecting the coordinator=E2=80=99s existing target as=
signment.



