Prakhar Kulshrestha created KAFKA-21241:
-------------------------------------------

             Summary: Increase the number of consumers in the share consume=
r group
                 Key: KAFKA-21241
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21241
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Prakhar Kulshrestha


Currently the max =C2=A0number of consumers in a share consumer group is de=
fault to 200 and max to 1000. =C2=A0In bigger platforms where batch process=
ing along with slow consumer use cases limiting to just 1000 consumer is ve=
ry restrictive.{*}{*}

One of the scenario is a batch processing of millions of records and having=
 to parallel process 20-30k records in parallel using spring kafka concurre=
ncy feature would mean we would need at least 20-30k consumers in a consume=
r groups with around 1k pods. Current 1000 limit just let it have ~60pods.

Request this to be reevaluated and increase the number of consumers that a =
share group can have.

*group.share.max.size*



