sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21244:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Server-side consumer regex subscriptions do not honor=
 `exclude.internal.topics`
                 Key: KAFKA-21244
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21244
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


*Description*

When using {{SubscriptionPattern}} with {{{}*group.protocol=3Dconsumer*{}}}=
, server-side regex subscriptions do not honor {{{}*exclude.internal.topics=
=3Dtrue*{}}}. The same issue occurs when the configuration is omitted, sinc=
e its default value is {{{}true{}}}.

*Java {{Pattern}}* subscriptions correctly exclude internal topics under th=
e same consumer protocol. This creates inconsistent configuration behavior =
between the two regex subscription APIs.

=C2=A0

*Conditions*
 * {{group.protocol=3Dconsumer}}
 * {{{}exclude.internal.topics=3Dtrue{}}}, or the configuration is omitted
 * A regex that also matches internal topic names, such as {{SubscriptionPa=
ttern(".*")}}
 * An internal topic, such as {{{}__consumer_offsets{}}}, exists in the coo=
rdinator metadata
 * The consumer has the required permissions to describe and read the topic

Example configuration and subscription:
{code:java}
props.put("group.protocol", "consumer");
props.put("exclude.internal.topics", "true");

consumer.subscribe(new SubscriptionPattern(".*")); {code}
=C2=A0

*Expected Behavior*

Internal topics should be excluded from the subscription and assignment eve=
n when they match the regex.

With {{{}exclude.internal.topics=3Dfalse{}}}, matching internal topics shou=
ld remain eligible for subscription. Explicit subscriptions by topic name s=
hould also preserve the existing contract: internal topics may be explicitl=
y subscribed to even when the setting is {{{}true{}}}.

=C2=A0

*Observed Behavior and Cause*

For Java {{Pattern}} subscriptions, the client evaluates the regex against =
metadata that excludes internal topics and sends the matching topic names i=
n the heartbeat's {{SubscribedTopicNames}} field.

For {{SubscriptionPattern}} subscriptions, the client sends the regex strin=
g in {{{}SubscribedTopicRegex{}}}. The current heartbeat schema has no fiel=
d for conveying the internal-topic exclusion setting, and {{TopicRegexResol=
ver}} evaluates the regex against all topic names without excluding interna=
l topics.

Additionally, {{ConsumerMetadata.retainTopic(...)}} retains metadata for to=
pic IDs assigned through server-side regex subscriptions using the followin=
g condition:
{code:java}
return retainTopic(topicName, isInternal, nowMs)
    || subscription.isAssignedFromRe2j(topicId); {code}
Consequently, metadata is retained for a topic ID assigned by the server ev=
en when the internal-topic exclusion check returns {{{}false{}}}.



