Hi,

1. Yes I decided to ignore the null case, the configuration is either
set (and we call setNamedGroups) or empty (and we don't call
setNamedGroups). This is the same behavior than ciphers.
The only scenario I can think of when handling null would make sense
is to reset the named groups for a listener. For example, you set
ssl.named.groups=3Dx25519,x448, but then want a specific listener to use
all the default named groups. Without null you will need to set
listener.name.internal.ssl.named.groups to all the default named
groups. That seems a very niche scenario and I preferred keeping the
behavior consistent with ciphers.
For completeness I've added that option as a rejected alternative for
now unless the community expresses interest in it.

2. Yes that's an option.

Thanks,
Mickael


