Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21245) Support hex-encoded key/value in
 console consumer and producer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Chia-Ping Tsai (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21245:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Support hex-encoded key/value in console consumer and=
 producer
                 Key: KAFKA-21245
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21245
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


I was testing compacted topics and noticed that there is no official tool t=
o write a tombstone for a specific record. The console producer can produce=
 null values (KIP-810), but there is no way to type a binary key, so record=
s with serialized keys (long, Avro, Protobuf, etc.) cannot be deleted from =
the command line.

Of course, we can leverage AI to generate 1000 tools immediately, but =E2=
=80=9Cthis tool=E2=80=9D can be addressed by supporting hex =F0=9F=99=82

Also, hex is the baseline for all types of records. It is line-safe, so the=
 output can be piped through grep, awk, and other console tools, and it can=
 be fed back into the console producer to reproduce the exact same bytes.



