Hi Jiunn-Yang,

Thanks for running the release. I verified 4.3.2-rc1 as follows:

- Verified the SHA512 checksum and GPG signature of the source tarball.
  It is signed by Jiunn Yang Huang, whose key is in KEYS.
- Built from source with JDK 17 (./gradlew clean build -x test).
- Ran the clients and core unit tests: all passed with no retries
  (clients 13160 passed, core 2329 passed).
- Ran the full system tests on the rc1 commit (30e0c713):
  https://jenkins.opensource4you.tw/job/kafka-e2e/968/
  1116 tests, 1108 passed, 6 failed. I checked the logs of all 6
  failures. None of them is related to the changes in rc1. They look
  like environment or timing issues: share consumer benchmark timeouts,
  a slow KRaft controller during topic creation, a missed log line in
  the Streams smoke test, and an out-of-memory error in the producer
  benchmark tool. Similar failures also happened in the rc0 run and in
  4.3 branch runs.

I also agree with doing another RC for the Jackson fixes. I will run
the same checks on the next RC.

Best,
Eric

