Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21251) kafka-streams-groups.sh --describe
 --topology: global store sub-topology label can collide with a real
 subtopology id
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Alieh Saeedi (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Alieh Saeedi created KAFKA-21251:
------------------------------------

             Summary: kafka-streams-groups.sh --describe --topology: global=
 store sub-topology label can collide with a real subtopology id
                 Key: KAFKA-21251
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21251
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Alieh Saeedi


h2. Problem

{{TopologyDescriptionFormatter}} (tools/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/tool=
s/streams/TopologyDescriptionFormatter.java) labels global stores starting =
at {{{}topology.subtopologies().size(){}}}:
=C2=A0
=C2=A0{{int globalStoreId =3D topology.subtopologies().size();for (final Gl=
obalStore globalStore : topology.globalStores()) {    appendGlobalStore(sb,=
 globalStore, globalStoreId++);}}}
This assumes regular subtopologies are numbered {{{}0..N-1{}}}. In Kafka St=
reams, global stores and subtopologies share one node-group id counter ({{{=
}InternalTopologyBuilder{}}}), so if the app defines its global store/table=
 first, the global store gets id {{0}} and regular subtopologies get {{{}1.=
.N{}}}.
h2. Example

Global store defined first, then two regular subtopologies (real ids 1, 2).=
 CLI output:
=C2=A0
=C2=A0{{Sub-topology: 1Sub-topology: 2Sub-topology: 2 for global store (wil=
l not generate tasks)   <- collides with real sub-topology 2}}
Stock Streams {{TopologyDescription.toString()}} would label the global sto=
re {{{}0{}}}.
h2. Impact

Cosmetic, CLI display only (KIP-1331 {{{}--describe --topology{}}}). Stored=
/pushed topology data and the CRD are unaffected. Not a release blocker; ca=
n confuse operators reading the output.
h2. Possible fixes
 # Minimal: start global labels at {{max(subtopology id) + 1}} =E2=80=94 re=
moves the collision, but may still differ from Streams' own id.

 # Exact: carry the global store's real id in the KIP-1331 description and =
print it =E2=80=94 matches stock Streams output, but needs a protocol/API c=
hange.



--
