Chia-Ping Tsai resolved KAFKA-21110.
------------------------------------
    Fix Version/s: 4.5.0
       Resolution: Fixed

> Document that min.insync.replicas is bounded by the replica count
> -----------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-21110
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21110
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
>            Assignee: Lucy Liu
>            Priority: Minor
>             Fix For: 4.5.0
>
>
> {code:java}
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 public static final String MIN_IN_SYNC_REPLICAS_CONFIG =3D =
"min.insync.replicas";
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 public static final String MIN_IN_SYNC_REPLICAS_DOC =3D "Sp=
ecifies the <i>minimum</i> number of in-sync replicas (including the leader=
) " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "required for a write to succeed when a produ=
cer sets <code>acks</code> to \"all\" (or \"-1\"). In the <code>acks=3Dall<=
/code> " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "case, every in-sync replica must acknowledge=
 a write for it to be considered successful. E.g., if a topic has " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "<code>replication.factor</code> of 3 and the=
 ISR set includes all three replicas, then all three replicas must acknowle=
dge an " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "<code>acks=3Dall</code> write for it to succ=
eed, even if <code>min.insync.replicas</code> happens to be less than 3. " =
+
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "If <code>acks=3Dall</code> and the current I=
SR set contains fewer than <code>min.insync.replicas</code> members, then t=
he producer " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "will raise an exception (either <code>NotEno=
ughReplicas</code> or <code>NotEnoughReplicasAfterAppend</code>).<br> " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "Regardless of the <code>acks</code> setting,=
 the messages will not be visible to the consumers until " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "they are replicated to all in-sync replicas =
and the <code>min.insync.replicas</code> condition is met.<br> " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "When used together, <code>min.insync.replica=
s</code> and <code>acks</code> allow you to enforce greater durability guar=
antees. " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "A typical scenario would be to create a topi=
c with a replication factor of 3, " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "set <code>min.insync.replicas</code> to 2, a=
nd produce with <code>acks</code> of \"all\". " +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "This ensures that a majority of replicas mus=
t persist a write before it's considered successful by the producer and it'=
s visible to consumers." +
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "<p>Note that when the Eligible Leader Replic=
as feature is enabled, the semantics of this config changes. Please refer t=
o <a href=3D\"https://kafka.apache.org/documentation/#eligible_leader_repli=
cas\">the ELR section</a> for more info.</p>";
>  {code}
> Since 3.7.0 (#14594, part of KIP-966), the broker uses {{min(min.insync.r=
eplicas, replica count)}} as the effective min ISR. This applies to both {{=
acks=3Dall}} produce requests and the high watermark advancement, and it is=
 not related to whether ELR is enabled.
> The current doc does not mention this, and it still says the producer get=
s {{NotEnoughReplicas}} when the ISR is smaller than {{{}min.insync.replica=
s{}}}. The ELR note also implies the semantics change with ELR, but the ELR=
 section only covers config management rules ...



