            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


{code:java}
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 int getTopicEffectiveMinIsr(String topicName) {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 String minIsrConfig =3D configurationControl.ge=
tTopicConfig(topicName, MIN_IN_SYNC_REPLICAS_CONFIG).value();
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 int currentMinIsr =3D Integer.parseInt(minIsrCo=
nfig);
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 Uuid topicId =3D topicsByName.get(topicName);
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 int replicationFactor =3D topics.get(topicId).p=
arts.get(0).replicas.length;
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 return Math.min(currentMinIsr, replicationFacto=
r);
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 } {code}
Since each partition is allowed to have different replicas, the incorrect r=
eplica number could clear the ELR unexpectedly. For example, the first part=
ition has only 1 replica, so the controller assumes the HW can be advanced =
(due to min ISR =3D 1) and clears the ELR set.



