ryType.orNull)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 } {code}
We don=E2=80=99t parse all broker-related values in KafkaConfig. For exampl=
e, the cluster-wide and prefixed configs. Hence, we catch the =E2=80=9Craw =
string=E2=80=9D and then keep it as it is to avoid casting error.

However, we don=E2=80=99t even have such tests for both cases. #23785 remov=
ed the guard and CI was still green. We should add integration tests for de=
scribing a cluster-wide LIST config (e.g. {{{}log.cleanup.policy{}}}) and a=
