Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-21270:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Race condition can cause a newly created connector to=
 use initial offsets from another request
                 Key: KAFKA-21270
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21270
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


{{doPutConnectorConfig}} needs two requests to complete its job, which mean=
s another user=E2=80=99s request could slip in between and cause a race con=
dition. For example, the first request sets initial offsets, but the second=
 doesn=E2=80=99t. When the race happens, the connector created by the secon=
d request could use the initial offsets set by the first request without an=
y warning.

Of course ... if both requests have identical initial offsets, that is fine=
 =F0=9F=99=82



