Hi Jiunn-Yang,

Thanks for running the 4.3.2 release.

I did the following to validate RC3:

- Verified checksums (md5/sha1/sha512) and GPG signatures
  - Artifacts: source, binary, site-docs, RELEASE_NOTES
  - Signed by Jiunn Yang Huang <jyhuang@apache.org>
  - Key 062C22C0F467AF9A02D512B5504473FAF80CBBCB
- Verified GPG signatures of the Maven staging artifacts
  - 65 modules, all signed with the same key as the tarballs
- Built from source with JDK 17
  - Ran the core, clients and streams unit tests
- Ran quickstarts from the bundled site-docs against the binary dist
  - Broker quickstart
  - Kafka Streams WordCount quickstart
  - Used both the classic and streams (KIP-1071) group protocols
- Ran the same quickstarts against the Docker images
  - apache/kafka:4.3.2-rc3
  - apache/kafka-native:4.3.2-rc3
- Checked shipped jar versions for the dependency and CVE bumps
  - jackson-core and jackson-databind 2.21.7
  - log4j 2.25.5
  - jetty 12.0.37
  - lz4-java 1.11.4
  - snappy-java 1.1.10.11
- Exercised the rc3 dependency bumps against a local broker
  - lz4/snappy/zstd/gzip round trips, incl. broker recompression
  - Connect REST and partition reassignment JSON (Jackson)
- Exercised these fixes by hand, comparing against 4.3.1
  - Clients:
    - KAFKA-20700, KAFKA-20769
  - Streams:
    - KAFKA-20464
  - Group coordinator:
    - KAFKA-20434

- Docs still reference 4.3.1 quickstart etc - not a blocker we can do a
follow-up PR.

+1 (binding)

Thanks,
Bill

