Hi Jiunn-Yang,

Thanks for running the release. I verified 4.3.2-rc3 as follows:

- Verified the SHA512 checksums and GPG signatures of the source and
  binary tarballs. They are signed by Jiunn Yang Huang, whose key is
  in KEYS.
- Built from source with JDK 17 (./gradlew clean build -x test).
- Ran the clients and core unit tests. All core tests passed. One
  clients test failed once (SaslAuthenticatorTest
  .testValidSaslScramMechanisms). It passed in 5 reruns, and
  SaslAuthenticatorTest is already flaky on Develocity, so I think it
  is a flaky test.
- Started a KRaft broker from the binary tarball with JDK 17. Produced
  and consumed with none, gzip, snappy, lz4 and zstd compression.
- Started apache/kafka:4.3.2-rc3 and apache/kafka-native:4.3.2-rc3
  with the default config (using podman). Produce and consume work on
  both.
- Ran the full system tests on the rc3 commit (0a6c96d3):
  https://jenkins.opensource4you.tw/job/kafka-e2e/975/
  1116 tests, 1103 passed, 11 failed. I checked the logs of all 11
  failures. They are known flaky tests or timing issues, and none of
  them is related to this release.

+1 (non-binding)

Best,
Eric

