Gavin Wang created KAFKA-21273:
----------------------------------

             Summary: Improve refiner performance
                 Key: KAFKA-21273
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21273
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Gavin Wang
            Assignee: Gavin Wang


We landed the first version of the refiner w/o any JMH results. If we need =
to optimize for better performance a few ideas to explore (some already dis=
cussed during code review):
 * replace Java Streams API usage with =E2=80=9Cnative=E2=80=9D loops

 * replace list+sort with heap

 * cache more helper data structures (cf below)

 * maybe integrate deeper with reconciler

About helper data structures: currently, the GC uses an in-memory cache to =
store the intermediate assignment. We could extent this, to also store help=
er data structures like =E2=80=9Cload index=E2=80=9D which change increment=
ally for most cases, and we should be able to re-used across refiner runs (=
atm, the refiner computes all helpers from scratch on each run). Other cand=
idates for caching is =E2=80=9Cfunding candidate order=E2=80=9D (ie, in whi=
ch order we plan to assign warmup tasks =E2=80=94 it=E2=80=99s mainly load =
based so keeping it across refiner runs and maintaining it incrementally mi=
ght also cut costs; for this case, a heap might become really beneficial).



