Gergely Harmad=C3=A1s created KAFKA-21274:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: Remove unused javax jaxb-api and activation dependenc=
ies
                 Key: KAFKA-21274
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21274
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Task
          Components: connect
            Reporter: Gergely Harmad=C3=A1s
            Assignee: Gergely Harmad=C3=A1s


{{javax.activation:activation}} and {{javax.xml.bind:jaxb-api}} are declare=
d in a few places in build.gradle with the comment
{quote}Jersey dependency that was available in the JDK before Java 9
{quote}
This is a stale comment as Jersey is 3.1.x uses the jakarta namespace and a=
lready resolves (transitively) {{com.sun.activation:jakarta.activation}} an=
d {{{}jakarta.xml.bind:jakarta.xml.bind-api{}}}.

In Kafka 4.0 the project was migrated to Jakarta with [KIP-1032|https://cwi=
ki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/298781371/KIP-1032+Upgrade+to+J=
akarta+and+JavaEE+10+in+Kafka+4.0] and KAFKA-16437 so the two remaining jav=
ax dependencies should be safe to remove. Verified with :trogdor:test, :con=
nect:mirror:test (including
the MirrorMaker integration tests) and the :connect:runtime REST tests.

Next to the benefit of handling less dependencies we can remove 3 jars from=
 the released artifact and shave off around ~247 KB in size.
 * {{jaxb-api-2.3.1.jar}}
 * {{activation-1.1.1.jar}}
 * {{javax.activation-api-1.2.0.jar}}

Note that in theory there can be a few connector which relied on having jax=
b and activation on the classpath from Kafka. However [KIP-1032|https://cwi=
ki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/298781371/KIP-1032+Upgrade+to+J=
akarta+and+JavaEE+10+in+Kafka+4.0] already calls out this scenario
{quote}Users that use the Connect framework will need to upgrade their cust=
om connectors to use the new jakarta namespace (if they rely on it) or else=
 will need to use an isolated classloader.
{quote}



