Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21277) Docker image: support KRaft dynamic
 quorum (KIP-853) controllers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Maros Orsak (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Maros Orsak created KAFKA-21277:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Docker image: support KRaft dynamic quorum (KIP-853) =
controllers
                 Key: KAFKA-21277
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21277
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Maros Orsak
            Assignee: Maros Orsak


The Docker image can only run controllers with static voters. With controll=
er.quorum.bootstrap.servers instead:
 # KafkaDockerWrapper always formats with plain kafka-storage format. On a =
controller without voters, StorageTool requires --standalone or --no-initia=
l-controllers, so the format fails and the container exits.
 # The image configure script rejects KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS on control=
ler-only nodes, but a dynamic voter needs an advertised controller endpoint=
.

=C2=A0

We should (i.) add a new env var (e.g. STORAGE_FORMAT_ARGS) appended to the=
 images format command and (ii.) allow KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS on contro=
llers when it lists only controller listeners.

Default behaviour stays unchanged. Since the env vars are part of the image=
s, interface (KIP-975), this might require a small KIP.

Affects the 3.9.x+ version.



