Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21283) Fix StreamThreadTest teardown race
 causing thread leaks and cascading test failures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Ken Huang (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Ken Huang created KAFKA-21283:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Fix StreamThreadTest teardown race causing thread lea=
ks and cascading test failures
                 Key: KAFKA-21283
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21283
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Test
            Reporter: Ken Huang
            Assignee: Ken Huang


`StreamThreadTest.tearDown()` directly calls `TaskManager.shutdown(false)` =
before requesting `StreamThread` shutdown. For tests that start a real `Str=
eamThread`, this can race with the thread while it is draining restored tas=
ks from `StateUpdater`.

In `shouldRecoverFromInvalidOffsetExceptionOnRestoreAndFinishRestore(true)`=
, this can cause shutdown to request removal of a task that the `StreamThre=
ad` has already taken, resulting in:

```text
IllegalStateException: Task 0_0 was not found in the state updater.
```

The exception interrupts cleanup before StateUpdater and TaskExecutor shutd=
own, and skips the subsequent StreamThread shutdown request. The remaining =
TaskExecutor then causes later tests in the same JVM to fail their thread l=
eak checks. The observed report contains one initial cleanup failure follow=
ed by 31 such failures.

Update teardown to request shutdown and join started StreamThreads, allowin=
g them to clean up their TaskManager through their normal shutdown path. Pr=
eserve manual TaskManager cleanup for threads that were never started but w=
hose Streams state was advanced by the test.


