<dev@kafka.apache.org> wrote:
>
> Hi Luke,   Thanks for reviewing the KIP.   Regarding LC1, that makes sens=
e. The tests can run on all supported Java versions rather than skipping th=
e unsupported case entirely. On Java 20 and later, they can verify that con=
figured named groups are applied. On earlier Java versions, a non-empty ssl=
.named.groups can be tested to ensure that creating the SSL engine throws a=
n InvalidConfigurationException. Empty or unset configurations should conti=
nue to work without calling SSLParameters.setNamedGroups(). I=E2=80=99ll up=
date the PR tests accordingly.   Regarding LC2, my understanding is that a =
non-empty ssl.named.groups is an explicit Kafka configuration and is applie=
d to each Kafka-created SSL engine through SSLParameters.setNamedGroups(). =
It therefore takes precedence over the JVM-wide jdk.tls.namedGroups value f=
or those engines. When ssl.named.groups is empty or unset, Kafka does not c=
all setNamedGroups(), so the JVM system propertyor the provider defaults wh=
en that property is absentcontinues to apply.   I agree that this precedenc=
e should be stated explicitly in the compatibility section. I don=E2=80=99t=
 think Kafka needs to reject or warn when both are configured, since the Ka=
fka-specific setting is presumably an intentional per-application override,=
 but it would be useful to document the behavior clearly.
> Thanks and regardsArnab Nandy
>
>     On Thursday, 15 October 2026 at 01:00:48 pm IST, Luke Chen <showuon@g=
mail.com> wrote:
>
>  Hi Mickael,
> Thanks for the KIP!This is necessary to protect connections in kafka.
> LC1: "These tests will be skipped when run on a JVM that does not support=
 named groups. The CI already runs with Java 25, so this will be effectivel=
y tested."I'm wondering if we can run tests with all java versions, but exp=
ect to fail when running on unsupported versions? If we only test java 25, =
we can't test the unsupported java version with ConfigExceptions, right?
> LC2: About the jvm "jdk.tls.namedGroups" system properties:LC2.1. What if=
 current users already set "jdk.tls.namedGroups=3Dx25519" system properties=
, and after this KIP, it also sets "ssl.named.groups=3Dx448", then I think =
the jvm system properties will be skipped, right? Do you think this will ca=
use some unexpected security problems? Maybe when setting "ssl.named.groups=
", we should check if "jdk.tls.namedGroups" system properties are set or no=
t?LC2.2. In the compatibility section, I think we should add some explanati=
ons about how we honor "ssl.named.groups" and "jdk.tls.namedGroups" when ea=
ch is set or not set.
>
> Thank you,Luke
