Omnia Ibrahim created KAFKA-21290:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Add ASF allowlist check to CI workflows
                 Key: KAFKA-21290
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21290
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Omnia Ibrahim


When a workflow references a GitHub Action that isn=E2=80=99t on the ASF or=
g-level allowlist, the job dies at startup with no logs and the PR can stil=
l look green =E2=80=94 nothing actually ran. We=E2=80=99ve been finding out=
 about this the hard way, after the fact, when a pin drifts off the approve=
d list.

ASF Infra ships a composite action for exactly this =E2=80=94 {{{}apache/in=
frastructure-actions/allowlist-check{}}}=E2=80=94 that scans every {{uses:}=
} ref under {{.github/}} and checks it against the approved allowlist (with=
 the GitHub/ASF-owned orgs {{{}actions/*{}}}, {{{}github/*{}}}, {{apache/*}=
} implicitly trusted). It also warns when an approved pin is nearing its up=
stream expiry, which is the usual cause of the silent failures.

This adds a small workflow wiring that action in, so we catch an unapproved=
 or expiring action at PR time instead of mid-CI. It runs on PRs and on a w=
eekly schedule =E2=80=94 the schedule covers the case where an allowlisted =
pin expires upstream in a week where we don=E2=80=99t touch {{{}.github/{}}=
}.

Already in use across other ASF projects (Storm,Lucene, Iceberg), and Infra=
 auto-PRs it into major repos, so this just brings Kafka in line with the s=
tandard setup.



