{code:java}
  =C2=A0 public synchronized void unsubscribe() {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.subscription =3D Collections.emptySet();
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.groupSubscription =3D Collections.emptySet=
();
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.assignment.clear();
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.assignedTopicIds =3D Collections.emptySet(=
);
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.subscribedPattern =3D null;
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.subscriptionType =3D SubscriptionType.NONE=
;
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.listenerContext.set(ListenerContext.NULL_L=
ISTENER); // this=20
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 this.assignmentId++;
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 } {code}
The previous logic did not reset the listener, and {{setRebalanceListener}}=
 is the only method meant to set or remove it (passing {{{}null{}}}). KIP-1=
306 does not say {{unsubscribe()}} should clear the listener either.



