{code:java}
3. Configure SASL port and SASL mechanisms in server.properties as describe=
d here. For example:=C2=A0=C2=A0 =C2=A0```java-properties
=C2=A0 =C2=A0listeners=3DSASL_SSL://host.name:port
=C2=A0 =C2=A0security.inter.broker.protocol=3DSASL_SSL
=C2=A0 =C2=A0sasl.mechanism.inter.broker.protocol=3DOAUTHBEARER
=C2=A0 =C2=A0sasl.enabled.mechanisms=3DOAUTHBEARER
=C2=A0 =C2=A0listener.name.<listener name>.oauthbearer.sasl.server.callback=
.handler.class=3Dorg.apache.kafka.common.security.oauthbearer.OAuthBearerVa=
lidatorCallbackHandler
=C2=A0 =C2=A0listener.name.<listener name>.oauthbearer.sasl.oauthbearer.jwk=
s.endpoint.url=3Dhttps://example.com/oauth2/v1/keys
=C2=A0 =C2=A0listener.name.<listener name>.oauthbearer.sasl.oauthbearer.exp=
ected.audience=3Dmy-kafka-cluster
=C2=A0 =C2=A0listener.name.<listener name>.oauthbearer.sasl.oauthbearer.exp=
ected.issuer=3Dhttps://example.com
=C2=A0 =C2=A0``` {code}
The internal communication is using OAUTHBEARER, but it doesn't set the log=
in callback. Hence, the broker won't have the token, which results in failu=
re.



