Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21295) Kafka Producer stalls when crossing
 seqnum 2^31 with MESSAGE_TOO_LARGE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Chris (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Chris created KAFKA-21295:
-----------------------------

             Summary: Kafka Producer stalls when crossing seqnum 2^31 with MESSAGE_TOO_LARGE
                 Key: KAFKA-21295
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21295
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: producer 
    Affects Versions: 4.2.2
            Reporter: Chris
            Assignee: Chris


ProducerBatch.split() assigns sequences to the split pieces with raw integer addition. KAFKA-7693 fixed an overflow bug in the normal send path, but not in this function. So when a producer's per-partition sequence is near 2^31 and a batch straddling the wrap is rejected with MESSAGE_TOO_LARGE and split, one piece receives a negative base sequence.



