Lianet Magrans created KAFKA-21296:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: OAuth login calls do not apply default timeouts as de=
fined in KIP-768
                 Key: KAFKA-21296
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21296
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: clients
            Reporter: Lianet Magrans


The client configs sasl.login.connect.timeout.ms and sasl.login.read.timeou=
t.ms are optional, defined without defaults in the code, and set only when =
defined by the app, here [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/8e65883c1255=
f93361bbf29efa8425e30b40c5ec/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/=
security/oauthbearer/internals/secured/HttpJwtRetriever.java#L212-L216]=C2=
=A0

KIP-768 does define default values for them (10000 ms), but the implementat=
ion does not seem to consider them, so if not set by the app, calls to conn=
ect/read to the token endpoint would run without explicit boundaries I expe=
ct (so hang if the token endpoint does not respond promptly).=C2=A0

Login calls are triggred from the clients constructors, so I expect the han=
g could happen when creating them (this login https://github.com/apache/kaf=
ka/blob/8e65883c1255f93361bbf29efa8425e30b40c5ec/clients/src/main/java/org/=
apache/kafka/common/security/authenticator/LoginManager.java#L69)

This Jira is to review this path and fix by applying the defaults proposed =
by KIP-798.



