Hi Mickael,

Thanks for the KIP. It=E2=80=99s good to see Kafka take on the PQC world; I h=
ad a few comments.

AK1: nit: but the Status is still marked as Draft and the Discussion Link is=
 still TBD

AK2: The reflection mechanism could use some details. Are we storing a Metho=
dHandle reference when DefaultSslEngineFactory initializes in a static block=
?

AK3: If the contract is to throw ConfigException because of missing names gr=
oup support on the jdk, there=E2=80=99s nothing in the SslEngineFactory to h=
ave other engines follow the spec. ssl.engine.factory.class for other engine=
s won=E2=80=99t adhere to this, and may break silently after launch.

AK4: Should we file a JIRA in conjunction to deprecate/cleanup the reflectio=
n once all clients and servers update their minimum supported version >=3D 2=
0?

AK5:=20
> a TLS connection can only be established when the client and server share a=
t least one named group

I see in other replies than this would this be an sslhandshakexception that t=
he jdk SSLEngine throws. Would it be worth adding a custom KafkaException th=
at suggests to users on the supported named groups in the current VM via SSL=
Context.getSupportedSSLParameters().getNamedGroups(). We sometimes do this w=
hen serialization fails, max poll interval elapses etc.

AK6: On Testing, there=E2=80=99s a negative test that we=E2=80=99re missing.=
 We can ensure assertThrows(ConfigException.class) on jdk versions < 20 whic=
h maybe a lot of the clients out there.

AK7: I think for the simplicity alone, reflection is what we might settle on=
. But I wanted to call out that there=E2=80=99s technically another approach=
 that might get us there without it.
We could do a multi-release JAR which has been available since jdk9. We can c=
reate a custom java20 source set and have gradle include it in the build.=20=

We can define a plain class on the base layer as
```java
public class NamedGroupSupport {
    public boolean supported() { return false; }
    public void apply(SSLParameters sslParams, String[] groups) { throw new U=
nsupportedOperationException(); }
}
```
And in the java20 source set, have the right implementation. We also need=20=

```groovy
jar {
   into(=E2=80=98META-INF/versions/20=E2=80=99) { from sourceSets.java20.out=
put }
  manifest { attributes =E2=80=98Multi-Release=E2=80=99: =E2=80=98true=E2=80=
=99 }
}
```
With the above in addition to a custom java20 source set with options.releas=
e =3D 20 could get us there for free.=20

But the cost is the build complexity, if someone shades the kafka-clients JA=
R they lose support. Also for clients who fork and build their own JARs this=
 would not be preferable. So overall, reflection is the simpler answer I thi=
nk but an alternative nonetheless to reject imo.

Thanks,
Aditya Kousik

