Hi Arnab,
thanks for the KIP and for starting this discussion.

As I mentioned when we looked at your PR
https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23310#issuecomment-5805162526

There have ben previous attempts at improving the policies interfaces:

https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/71012345/KIP-170+Enhanced+TopicCreatePolicy+and+introduction+of+TopicDeletePolicy
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/73637960/KIP-201+Rationalising+Policy+interfaces

Personally I think that adding methods to the current policy for
working around the inconsistency of the arguments isn't optimal.
We keep the limitations of the polices but with a wider interface that
we must support for backwards compatibility.
I would like to see a KIP expanding the capabilities of the policy
check, rather than just fixing the arguments for the different Alter
config operations.

Thanks,
Edo

