On 2026-10-16 02:30 UTC Eric Chang wrote:
> Hi all,
>=20
> While working on the bytes-based version of KIP-1325 with Murali, I looked
> at where the restore buffer actually grows.
>=20
> In StoreChangelogReader, records that can be applied are applied right after
> they are polled. Whether the buffer grows depends on the task type and on
> which topic the store uses as its changelog:
>=20
> - Active task, own changelog topic: it restores up to the end offset and
> applies every record it polls. The buffer does not grow.
> - Active task, input topic as changelog: it restores up to the committed
> offset and then finishes restoring. The buffer does not grow.
> - Standby task, own changelog topic: there is no limit, so it applies every
> record it polls. The buffer does not grow.
> - Standby task, input topic as changelog: it may only apply records up to
> the offset committed by the active task, but it keeps fetching beyond it.
> The buffer grows with every poll. This is the only case that can lead to
> an OutOfMemoryError, for example during a backfill.
>=20
> A store uses the input topic as its changelog when it comes from
> builder.table() and topology.optimization is set to "all" or
> "reuse.ktable.source.topics".
>=20
> Before 2.5.0, Streams paused such a standby partition. This was lost in the
> refactoring of KAFKA-9113. I opened KAFKA-21276 and a PR to restore that
> behavior, with no new config:
> https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23815
>=20
> If this is the only case where the restore buffer grows, the limit in
> KIP-1325 would never be reached after the fix. So I'd like to ask: do we
> still need a configurable limit for the restore buffer, for example as a
> safety net together with KIP-770, or is the fix enough?
>=20
> Karsten has since shared his configs on KAFKA-19992. He builds the topology
> with topology.optimization=3Dall and num.standby.replicas=3D1, and a heap d=
ump
> from his case showed StoreChangelogReader#changelogs holding more than 80%
> of the heap. So this looks like his case. I also reproduced it with a
> Debezium setup similar to his (600k records of 2 KB, -Xmx1g): with
> topology.optimization=3Dall the standby ran out of memory in all runs on
> trunk, and in none with the fix.
>=20
> Thanks,
> Eric
>=20

