Hi Edoardo,
Thanks for the feedback and for pointing me back to KIP-170 and KIP-201.
I understand the concern. Adding deletedConfigs() and configsWithoutNullVal=
ues() solves the immediate inconsistency, but it also extends an interface =
whose request model still does not clearly distinguish:
- the operations explicitly requested by the client;- the configuration bef=
ore the request; and- the configuration that would exist after the request.
That leaves similar limitations for SET, APPEND, SUBTRACT, legacy AlterConf=
igs, and future configuration operations.
Instead of adding more methods to the existing RequestMetadata, I=E2=80=99m=
 open to revising KIP-1382 around a new policy contract while leaving Alter=
ConfigPolicy unchanged for compatibility. The new request metadata could ex=
pose the resource, request type, explicit operations, current configuration=
 state, and proposed configuration state. Explicit deletions would then be =
represented naturally rather than inferred from null values or generated re=
cords.
I would prefer to keep this KIP focused on configuration alterations rather=
 than revive the full scope of KIP-201, which also covered topic creation, =
deletion, reassignment, partition changes, and record deletion. However, th=
e new contract can be designed so it does not repeat the limitations identi=
fied by KIP-201.
Would that focused successor to AlterConfigPolicy address your concern, or =
do you think the KIP should cover the broader topic-management policy model=
 as well?
Thanks,=C2=A0=C2=A0Arnab


Thanks and regardsArnab Nandy=20

    On Friday, 16 October 2026 at 09:13:23 pm IST, Edoardo Comar <edoardlis=
ts@gmail.com> wrote: =20
=20
 Hi Arnab,
thanks for the KIP and for starting this discussion.

As I mentioned when we looked at your PR
https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23310#issuecomment-5805162526

There have ben previous attempts at improving the policies interfaces:

https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/71012345/KIP-170+Enh=
anced+TopicCreatePolicy+and+introduction+of+TopicDeletePolicy
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/spaces/KAFKA/pages/73637960/KIP-201+Rat=
ionalising+Policy+interfaces

Personally I think that adding methods to the current policy for
working around the inconsistency of the arguments isn't optimal.
We keep the limitations of the polices but with a wider interface that
we must support for backwards compatibility.
I would like to see a KIP expanding the capabilities of the policy
check, rather than just fixing the arguments for the different Alter
config operations.

Thanks,
Edo

