sanghyeok An created KAFKA-21301:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Streams Group Assignment delays temporarily stop proc=
essing existing Streams tasks
                 Key: KAFKA-21301
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21301
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: sanghyeok An
            Assignee: sanghyeok An


With the KIP-1071 Streams Rebalance Protocol, when the assignment interval =
delays a new assignment computation, the coordinator returns {{ASSIGNMENT_D=
ELAYED}} while retaining the existing assignment.

Upon receiving this status, {{StreamsMembershipManager}} sets {{isGroupRead=
y=3Dfalse}} regardless of whether the member already has assigned tasks. Ev=
en when the task assignment is unchanged, the readiness change triggers an =
assignment callback, and {{DefaultStreamsRebalanceListener}} forwards the u=
pdated readiness to the StreamThread.

The default StreamThread processing loop returns before processing records =
when readiness is false. Consequently, existing tasks that could continue p=
rocessing are temporarily stopped while the next assignment computation is =
deferred.

A possible scenario is:
 # Member A has assigned tasks and is processing normally.
 # Member B joins, increasing the group epoch and requiring a new assignmen=
t computation.
 # The assignment interval has not elapsed since the last computation, so t=
he coordinator retains the existing target assignment. Member B waits witho=
ut a target assignment.
 # Member A sends a heartbeat during the same delay window. The coordinator=
 retains A=E2=80=99s existing assignment but also returns {{{}ASSIGNMENT_DE=
LAYED{}}}.
 # Member A sets readiness to false and stops processing its existing tasks=
.
 # Processing resumes after A receives a heartbeat response without the del=
ay status and completes the assignment callback.

This introduces an unnecessary processing gap despite unchanged task owners=
hip, potentially increasing record processing latency and reducing throughp=
ut. The default processing loop also skips punctuation and the commit stage=
 for that iteration.



