--000000000000faffac065e31e2ed
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

Hi all,

I believe I've found a bug in the Java consumer in kafka-clients 4.1 to
4.3.1.  A consumer using subscribe(SubscriptionPattern) stops sending Metadata
requests for good once a topic assigned to it is deleted. The client throws *an
*`IllegalStateException`*: "Use errorsByTopicId() when managing topic using
topic id"*, here
<https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.3.1/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/requests/MetadataResponse.java#L99>
, and after that, it never picks up new topics matching the pattern and
heartbeats until restarted.

I have a reproduction and have traced the cause, but I haven't been able to
file it yet. My ASF Jira account request (15th Oct) is still awaiting
approval.

Thanks,
James Palmer
Conduktor

