Evan Zhou created KAFKA-21311:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Throw when uncompressed records need more buffer space
                 Key: KAFKA-21311
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21311
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
            Reporter: Evan Zhou
            Assignee: Evan Zhou


For uncompressed batches, RecordAccumulator sizes the batch buffer before each append, so a write should never run past the buffer's capacity. In the case that this does happen, we should throw an exception instead of expanding so that we don't hide the underlying issue. 

https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23483/changes/BASE..a036ed99be4f2f38efc6d5def2961c72aed2af94#r4224404030



