Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21313) Share partition acquire fails with
 "Existing acquisition lock timeout exists" after a log start offset move
 splits a batch with a pending release
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Charles-Eddy (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Charles-Eddy created KAFKA-21313:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Share partition acquire fails with "Existing acquisit=
ion lock timeout exists" after a log start offset move splits a batch with =
a pending release
                 Key: KAFKA-21313
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21313
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: Charles-Eddy
         Attachments: 1-stale-acquisition-lock-after-split.patch

Hello, I found this while prototyping key-based ordering for share groups. =
It reproduces on plain trunk.

A released batch stays AVAILABLE with an ongoing state transition, and keep=
s its acquisition lock, until the persister write completes.

So if the log start offset moves inside that batch in the meantime (retenti=
on or DeleteRecords, seen through an OFFSET_OUT_OF_RANGE fetch), archiveRec=
ords splits it into per-offset states.

InFlightBatch.maybeInitializeOffsetStateUpdate() copies the batch lock to e=
very offset, including the AVAILABLE ones, and the ongoing transition is no=
t carried over, so the write completion never clears these locks.

The next acquire of one of these offsets moves it to ACQUIRED and then thro=
ws:
{code:java}
java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Existing acquisition lock timeout exist=
s, cannot override.
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.server.share.fetch.InFlightState.updateAc=
quisitionLockTimeoutTask(InFlightState.java:107)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at kafka.server.share.SharePartition.acquireSubsetBatchRecord=
s(SharePartition.java:2047)
  =C2=A0 at kafka.server.share.SharePartition.acquire(SharePartition.java:9=
50){code}
The ShareFetch request fails with UNKNOWN_SERVER_ERROR, and the record stay=
s ACQUIRED for a member that never received it until the stale lock expires=
. The timer task scheduled before the throw is left behind: in my runs it l=
ater released the record while another member was processing it.

The attached patch adds a test that reproduces it:SharePartitionTest#testRe=
leasedRecordsSplitByLogStartOffsetMoveWhileReleaseWriteIsPendingCanBeAcquir=
ed.

Not splitting a batch that has an ongoing transition (or carrying the trans=
ition over), and not copying the lock to offsets that are not ACQUIRED, sho=
uld fix it.



