Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21314) Share partition acquire throws
 "inconsistent range" at the in-flight limit on a compacted topic
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Charles-Eddy (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Charles-Eddy created KAFKA-21314:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Share partition acquire throws "inconsistent range" a=
t the in-flight limit on a compacted topic
                 Key: KAFKA-21314
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21314
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: Charles-Eddy
         Attachments: 2-inconsistent-range-at-in-flight-limit.patch

I found this while prototyping key-based ordering for share groups. It repr=
oduces on plain trunk.

When a share partition is at share.partition.max.record.locks, lastOffsetAn=
dMaxRecordsToAcquire caps lastOffsetToAcquire to the end offset. On a compa=
cted topic the records between the fetch offset and the end offset may be g=
one, so the first fetched batch can start after the end offset, and acquire=
() calls cachedState.subMap(from, to) with from > to:
{code:java}
java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: inconsistent range
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at java.base/java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentSkipListMap.subMa=
p(ConcurrentSkipListMap.java:1912)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at kafka.server.share.SharePartition.acquire(SharePartition.j=
ava:842){code}

In the simple case maybeArchiveStaleBatches has already archived the missin=
g offsets, so one ShareFetch request fails with UNKNOWN_SERVER_ERROR and th=
e partition recovers. After a re-initialization with a persister read gap a=
t the start of the window, the gap window does not advance and every fetch =
at the gap start fails the same way (I checked 3 consecutive fetches).

The attached patch adds a test for the simple case:SharePartitionTest#testA=
cquireAtMaxInFlightRecordsWhenAvailableRecordsAreCompactedAway.

Returning an empty result when the first fetched batch starts after lastOff=
setToAcquire, and moving the gap start past the compacted range, should fix=
 it, I don't know if it creates other issues though, I let you decide how t=
o solve this.



--
