Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21315) Share partition stops delivering
 records after an acknowledgement is rolled back below a moved start offset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Charles-Eddy (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Charles-Eddy created KAFKA-21315:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Share partition stops delivering records after an ack=
nowledgement is rolled back below a moved start offset
                 Key: KAFKA-21315
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21315
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: core
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: Charles-Eddy
         Attachments: 4-partition-stall-after-rolled-back-ack.patch

I found this while prototyping key-based ordering for share groups. It repr=
oduces on plain trunk.

If an ACCEPT is being written to the persister when the log start offset mo=
ves past the acknowledged batch (retention or DeleteRecords catching up wit=
h a lagging group), archiveRecords leaves the batch alone because it is not=
 AVAILABLE. If its acquisition lock then expires and the write fails, for e=
xample while the share coordinator is unavailable, completeStateTransition(=
false) moves the batch back to AVAILABLE, now below the start offset.

>From then on nextFetchOffset() returns that offset, the fetch fails with OF=
FSET_OUT_OF_RANGE, and updateCacheAndOffsets() returns early because the lo=
g start offset is not greater than the start offset. Every fetch logs "The =
log start offset: 6 is not greater than the start offset: 6 ..." and return=
s no records, so the records after the start offset are never delivered. On=
ly re-creating the SharePartition (leader change or broker restart) seems t=
o recover it.

The attached patch adds a test that reproduces it:SharePartitionTest#testAc=
ceptRolledBackAfterLockExpiryBelowMovedStartOffsetDoesNotStallFetches (next=
FetchOffset() returns 0 instead of 6).

The lock timeout path already archives records below the start offset. Doin=
g the same when a transition is rolled back with an expired lock should fix=
 it, and nextFetchOffset() could also skip offsets below the start offset. =
I let you decide what is the best way to handle that though.=C2=A0

=C2=A0

Thanks



