Gavin Wang created KAFKA-21321:
----------------------------------

             Summary: Streams group: the assignment refiner does not see a =
member that joins in the same heartbeat
                 Key: KAFKA-21321
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21321
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: group-coordinator, streams
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: Gavin Wang


h3. Problem
When a streams group heartbeat computes a new target assignment, \{{GroupMe=
tadataManager#refineAssignment}} passes \{{group.members()}} to the refiner=
 ([GroupMetadataManager:4707|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/f568b7b2c=
8802e6635b4d8df93ede88e55a2b84d/group-coordinator/src/main/java/org/apache/=
kafka/coordinator/group/GroupMetadataManager.java#L4707]). That map does no=
t contain the member sending the heartbeat yet, because the heartbeat's rec=
ords are replayed only after the handler returns. The target assignment the=
 refiner gets, however, comes from \{{UpdatedMembersAndTargetAssignmentView=
}}, which already adds that member, or relabels a replaced static member to=
 its new member ID ([:4583-4595|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/f568b7=
b2c8802e6635b4d8df93ede88e55a2b84d/group-coordinator/src/main/java/org/apac=
he/kafka/coordinator/group/GroupMetadataManager.java#L4583-L4595]).

So the refiner treats a target owner that joins in this heartbeat as a memb=
er that has left the group, and its result is cached as the epoch's interme=
diate assignment.

h3. Effects
With warm-up tasks enabled (the default), for stateful tasks:
# *A static member that rejoins under a new member ID gets none of its task=
s* when the same heartbeat computes a new target, for example because it re=
joins from a new process. The refiner keeps its active tasks on the old mem=
ber ID, which the replacement removes. The member is told nothing, and no m=
ember runs those tasks until the next refinement step.
# *A new member gets no warm-up task.* A stateful task the target moves to =
it stays on its old owner without a warm-up, even when warm-up slots are fr=
ee, until the next refinement step.
# *A task can run \{{num.standby.replicas + 1}} standbys.* If the new membe=
r is the target standby holder of a task whose migration borrows an existin=
g standby, its standby is not held back ([AssignmentRefinerImpl:866-872|htt=
ps://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/f568b7b2c8802e6635b4d8df93ede88e55a2b84d/=
group-coordinator/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/coordinator/group/streams/=
AssignmentRefinerImpl.java#L866-L872], [:818-823|https://github.com/apache/=
kafka/blob/f568b7b2c8802e6635b4d8df93ede88e55a2b84d/group-coordinator/src/m=
ain/java/org/apache/kafka/coordinator/group/streams/AssignmentRefinerImpl.j=
ava#L818-L823]). Once delivered it is kept, so the extra standby lasts unti=
l the migration completes.

The refiner's branches for a target owner missing from \{{members}} ([Assig=
nmentRefinerImpl:286-293|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/f568b7b2c8802=
e6635b4d8df93ede88e55a2b84d/group-coordinator/src/main/java/org/apache/kafk=
a/coordinator/group/streams/AssignmentRefinerImpl.java#L286-L293]) attribut=
e that case to assignment offloading and member fencing. Neither produces i=
t on trunk: streams assignor offloading is not wired up, and fencing remove=
s the member's target assignment together with the member. So today these b=
ranches fire only for a member that joins in the same heartbeat.

h3. Possible fix
Pass the view's members to the refiner, together with the view's target ass=
ignment.

h3. Reproduction
The test below fails on trunk (\{{46dc4b51f7}}) with \{{expected: <[TaskIds=
(subtopologyId=3D's1', partitions=3D[0])]> but was: <[]>}}. Place it in \{{=
group-coordinator/src/test/java/org/apache/kafka/coordinator/group/}}. Effe=
cts 2 and 3 reproduce the same way, with a joining dynamic member.

