Ojasva Jain created KAFKA-21323:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Remove deprecated java.util.regex fallback for client=
-metrics match patterns (KIP-714)
                 Key: KAFKA-21323
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21323
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 5.0.0
            Reporter: Ojasva Jain


KAFKA-15677 made client-metrics match patterns require RE2/J syntax, but ke=
pt a temporary fallback to java.util.regex (with a deprecation warning) for=
 pre-existing patterns, to avoid breaking subscriptions already persisted b=
efore this change. This is implemented via ClientMatchPattern.ofLegacy(...)=
 (@Deprecated(since =3D "4.5", forRemoval =3D true)) and ClientMetricsConfi=
gs.compileLenient(...).
=C2=A0
This ticket tracks removing that fallback in 5.0.0.
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
More context: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/23696#discussion_r433105=
4511



