Hi David,
Thanks for the KIP. Kafka is a complicated system and I am constantly
learning about it. I understand that rack-aware assignment is costly but
I am surprised that it only acts when fetch-from-follower is active.

I would have thought that the sweet spot for this is to assign partitions
for which the LEADER is in the client's rack. This is how I had envisaged
rack-aware assignment working for share consumers, which of course do not
support fetch-from-follower. The idea was to assign partitions to share
consumers in the same rack if possible, to avoid cross-rack consumption.
If we get around to rack-aware assignment for share groups, that's how it
will work.

Having a cluster-wide setting for disabling rack-aware assignments for
consumer groups and defaulting it to false suggests to me that rack-aware
assignment for consumer groups as specified doesn't really work as it
should. That may well be the case today :(

Thanks,
Andrew

