TengYao Chi created KAFKA-21325:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Enable asynchronous bootstrap DNS resolution by defau=
lt
                 Key: KAFKA-21325
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21325
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: TengYao Chi
            Assignee: TengYao Chi
             Fix For: 5.0.0


KIP-909 (KAFKA-14648) added \{{bootstrap.resolve.timeout.ms}}, which lets c=
lients
resolve bootstrap DNS asynchronously instead of blocking at construction. I=
t
currently defaults to \{{0}} (synchronous, original behavior), and https://=
issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20939
forces it off entirely in Connect and Streams after issues surfaced during
early adoption. As a result the feature has stayed opt-in rather than becom=
ing
the default.

This ticket tracks the work needed to responsibly enable it by default:

* Close remaining test coverage gaps around the async resolution path
=C2=A0 (retry/recovery behavior, and shutdown while a resolution is in flig=
ht).
* Decide on and implement proper support in Connect and Streams, which
=C2=A0 currently disable the feature outright.
* Re-evaluate the default value of \{{bootstrap.resolve.timeout.ms}} once t=
he
=C2=A0 above are addressed.

This is an umbrella/tracking ticket, work will happen in linked sub-tasks.



