Omnia Ibrahim created KAFKA-21328:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Add CI check for stale version references in docs/
                 Key: KAFKA-21328
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21328
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Omnia Ibrahim


Kafka's documentation under \{{docs/}} (Hugo source for kafka-site) contain=
s hardcoded version references in structured contexts:
 * Maven \{{<version>}} coordinates,
 * Docker image tags (\{{apache/kafka:X.Y.Z}}),
 * tarball/jar names (\{{kafka_2.13-X.Y.Z.tgz}}, {\{connect-file-X.Y.Z.jar}=
}),
 *  GitHub source links (\{{blob/X.Y/...}}),=20
 * archetype versions (\{{-DarchetypeVersion=3DX.Y.Z}}),
 * andjavadoc link titles ("Kafka X.Y Javadoc").

When a doc page is created by copy-pasting from an existing page (very comm=
on), these version strings are frequently carried over unchanged and never =
updated.

They then silently go stale until someone notices during a release =E2=80=
=94 e.g. the 4.4 docs still referenced 4.3 in numerous places, caught only =
by manual review during release staging.

I would like to propose an automated guard against this to prevent stale re=
ferences accumulate across a release cycle and land on the release manager =
at staging time =E2=80=94 the worst place to triage them, since the RM lack=
s the context for every line written months earlier by other contributors.

*Proposal:*

Add a CI check (new workflow + script under \{{.github/scripts/}}) that run=
s on any PR touching \{{docs/**}}, including on trunk (trunk is where most =
stale references are first introduced).

The check asserts that a small set of *high-signal, structured* version pat=
terns resolve to the current version (derived from \{{gradle.properties}}),=
 and flags any that point at a different, non-\{{trunk}} version:
 * =C2=A0\{{<version>X.Y.Z</version>}} and the sbt \{{% "X.Y.Z"}} form
 * {\{apache/kafka:X.Y.Z}}, \{{apache/kafka-native:X.Y.Z}}
 * {\{kafka_2.13-X.Y.Z.tgz}} / \{{kafka_2.13-X.Y.Z}}
 * {\{connect-file-X.Y.Z.jar}}, \{{kafka-storage-X.Y.Z-test.jar}}
 * {\{-DarchetypeVersion=3DX.Y.Z}}
 * {\{blob/X.Y/}} (allowing \{{blob/trunk/}})
 * "Kafka X.Y Javadoc"
 * {\{git checkout X.Y.Z}}



--
