 UpdateFeatures.max_version_level deletion semantics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Federico Valeri (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Federico Valeri created KAFKA-21332:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: Clarify UpdateFeatures.max_version_level deletion semantics
                 Key: KAFKA-21332
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21332
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Federico Valeri
            Assignee: Federico Valeri


The {{UpdateFeatures}} protocol documentation states that a {{max_version_level}} value less than {{1}} can be used to request deletion of the finalized feature. However, Kafka trunk rejects negative values and uses {{0}} to request deletion.

Update the protocol documentation to state explicitly that {{0}} requests deletion and negative values are invalid.



--
