Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21334) Test close() while async bootstrap
 DNS resolution is still pending
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "TengYao Chi (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

TengYao Chi created KAFKA-21334:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Test close() while async bootstrap DNS resolution is still pending
                 Key: KAFKA-21334
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21334
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Sub-task
          Components: clients
            Reporter: TengYao Chi
            Assignee: TengYao Chi


NetworkClient#close() cancels any pending bootstrap resolution and shuts down the kafka-bootstrap-dns-resolver executor. 
Every existing test that reaches close() under async bootstrap configuration does so only after the resolution has already failed/timed out, so this cancellation/shutdown path is unverified. 
Add a unit test that calls close() while a resolution is genuinely still pending.



--
