Subject: [DISCUSS] SslEngineFactory contract for dynamic SSL material (KIP-1288)
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
From: Henning Kvinnesland <henning.kvinnesland@gmail.com>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Hi Kafka developers,

I'm looking for clarification on the intended contract of the public
`SslEngineFactory` SPI, particularly in relation to dynamic SSL
credential rotation.

I recently contributed SSL bundle hot-reload support for Kafka clients
to Spring Boot (https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/pull/52257).
The Spring Boot team declined the proposal because it was unclear
whether relying on Kafka to create new `SSLEngine` instances using
dynamically updated key/trust material is an officially supported
behavior.

The implementation did not invoke `SslFactory.reconfigure()` or modify
Kafka internals. Instead, it supplied a stable `SslBundle` reference
that resolves the latest material whenever Kafka invokes
`SslEngineFactory.createClientSslEngine()`.

Could Kafka maintainers clarify whether the following is an intended
and supported use of the SPI?

- An `SslEngineFactory` dynamically resolves its key/trust material
whenever a new `SSLEngine` is requested.
- An existing producer/consumer continues running without recreation.
- Existing TLS connections remain unaffected, while subsequent
connections use renewed credentials.

This is narrower than KIP-1288, since file watching and certificate
rotation are already handled externally by Spring Boot.

I also noticed that KIP-1288 and PR #21488 have seen limited progress
since March. Is there a particular technical or design concern
preventing this work from moving forward, or is it mainly awaiting
maintainer review?

Related:
- https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/pull/52257
- https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/21488
- https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-10731
