Omnia Ibrahim created KAFKA-21347:
-------------------------------------

             Summary:  Add release.py blog subcommand to generate initial b=
log post
                 Key: KAFKA-21347
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21347
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: tools
            Reporter: Omnia Ibrahim


Today, {{release.py}} dispatches on three subcommands only: the default {{{=
}stage{}}}, {{{}stage-docs{}}}, and {{{}release-email{}}}. There is no {{bl=
og}} subcommand. The tooling automates two emails during a release =E2=80=
=94 the RC vote email and the release announcement email ({{{}release/templ=
ates.py{}}}: {{{}rc_vote_email_text{}}}, {{{}release_announcement_email{}}}=
) =E2=80=94 but the actual release announcement {*}blog post{*}(e.g. {{{}ka=
fka-site/content/en/blog/releases/ak-X.Y.Z.md{}}}) is still written entirel=
y by hand by the release manager for every release.



In practice, the release manager has to manually:
 # Create the blog post file with the correct frontmatter (date, title, slu=
g, author).
 # Re-derive and restate upgrade notes, notable changes, and KIPs in releas=
e plan

 # Cross-check version numbers, links, and contributor mentions by hand.

This is repetitive, error-prone (version/date typos, missed KIPs), and slow=
s down the release-week checklist.

=C2=A0

*Proposal:*

Add a command (e.g. {{{}./release.py generate-blog-post{}}}) that writes a =
skeleton {{ak-XYZ.md}} with:
 * Hugo front matter populated (title, date, author/RM, any required taxono=
my fields)
 * The standard section headings, in the standard order
 * Version strings and the release date substituted everywhere they appear
 * The contributor acknowledgement list, generated=C2=A0via the existing gi=
t helper in {{{}release/{}}}, deduped and sorted

 * A {{<!-- TODO -->}} marker in each body slot the RM must write



--
