=E2=80=99s=C2=A0{{bootstrap.servers}}=C2=A0at it, and it can inject error c=
odes, drop connections, or blackhole a client =E2=80=94 decoding/encoding w=
ith Kafka=E2=80=99s own protocol classes so it is correct across every wire=
 version (including flexible/tagged-field ones), no hand-rolled byte offset=
s.
> Placed in `clients/src/testFixtures` so it is reusable from any module. T=
his is internal test infrastructure only so it does not require a KIP.
> Fault primitives, each armed with a fluent, deterministic trigger:
> - `injectError(apiKey, Errors)` =E2=80=94 stamp an error code onto the ma=
tching response,
> =C2=A0 re-serialized at the correct wire version. Supported APIs: `END_TX=
N`,
> =C2=A0 `INIT_PRODUCER_ID`, `ADD_OFFSETS_TO_TXN`, `TXN_OFFSET_COMMIT`, `PR=
ODUCE`, `FETCH`
> =C2=A0 (extensible by registering a per-API setter).
> - `disconnectOn(apiKey)` =E2=80=94 drop the connection when the matching =
response would return
> =C2=A0 (models the EOS "commit gap"). Works on any API.
> - `delayOn(apiKey, Duration)` =E2=80=94 hold back the matching response t=
o model a slow broker,
> =C2=A0 isolated to that one connection.
> - `blackholeClient(clientIdSubstring)` =E2=80=94 drop all requests from a=
 targeted client before
> =C2=A0 the broker sees them, so the broker evicts it by session timeout (=
a reversible,
> =C2=A0 ungraceful one-node partition).
> Shared trigger DSL (`Occurrence`): `once()`, `onCall(n)`, `times(n)`, `ev=
eryTime()`,
> `withProbability(p)`. The deterministic triggers are safe for assertions;=
 probability is
> chaos-mode only. The proxy never closes sockets unless a `disconnectOn(..=
.)` rule fires,
> so it is not itself a source of flakiness. Rules can be armed/disarmed li=
ve from the test
> thread and each returns a handle exposing match/fire counts.



