Aditya Kousik created KAFKA-21350:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Per-call record limit for Consumer poll
                 Key: KAFKA-21350
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21350
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Aditya Kousik
            Assignee: Aditya Kousik


{{max.poll.records}}=C2=A0and=C2=A0{{max.poll.interval.ms}}=C2=A0are read w=
hen a consumer is constructed and neither can be changed=C2=A0afterwards.

If processing slows down,=C2=A0a batch that used to fit inside the poll int=
erval stops fitting.=C2=A0The consumer misses its=C2=A0deadline and leaves =
the group.=C2=A0The assignment is released through=C2=A0{{{}onPartitionsLos=
t{}}},=C2=A0so the in-flight batch was never=C2=A0committed and the next ow=
ner reprocesses it.

The consumer rejoins and asks for the same batch size without any changes t=
o config.=C2=A0It misses the deadline again.=C2=A0This continues until the =
slowdown ends.=C2=A0A shared dependency degrades for all members at once,=
=C2=A0so they hit it together=C2=A0and the group rebalances repeatedly.=C2=
=A0The common response is a process restart after increasing {{max.poll.int=
erval.ms}} or decreasing {{{}max.poll.records{}}}, which reassigns every gr=
oup in that JVM.



We can consider providing an API to lower the records from each poll operat=
ion to fit the best batch size that the client can currently deliver



