Hi all,

I'd like to start a discussion on KIP-1386, which lets an application set th=
e record limit on each call to poll() rather than only through max.poll.reco=
rds at construction.

When processing slows down, a batch sized for normal load stops fitting insi=
de max.poll.interval.ms. The consumer is evicted, rejoins, asks for another b=
atch, and is evicted again until the slowdown passes or the consumer is rest=
arted with larger max.poll.interval.ms (or smaller max.poll.records) often w=
ith an educated guess because there=E2=80=99s no visibility on how much the c=
onsumer missed the deadline by.

The KIP adds poll(PollOptions) with an optional maxRecords, bounded by max.p=
oll.records so a call can only ask for less. It also adds consumer metrics f=
or how much of the poll interval is left. It pairs with KIP-1364: once the r=
ebalance cause is exposed, an application evicted for exceeding the poll int=
erval can come back with a smaller batch.

Looking forward to your feedback.

KIP link: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/RwKDGw

Thanks,
Aditya=

