Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21354) kafka-metadata-quorum
 remove-controller output contains an extra space before "KRaft"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "akshatha ramesh (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

akshatha ramesh created KAFKA-21354:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: kafka-metadata-quorum remove-controller output contai=
ns an extra space before "KRaft"
                 Key: KAFKA-21354
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21354
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: tools
    Affects Versions: 4.2.2, 4.1.2, 4.0.2, 3.9.2, 4.3.2
         Environment: All platforms
            Reporter: akshatha ramesh


The success message printed by kafka-metadata-quorum.sh remove-controller c=
ontains two spaces before "KRaft".

Actual output:

Removed =C2=A0KRaft controller 2003 with directory id MkWfVYpS_qAWFaz7GuOkR=
g

The dry-run output has the same issue:

DRY RUN of removing =C2=A0KRaft controller 2003 with directory id MkWfVYpS_=
qAWFaz7GuOkRg

Expected output:

Removed KRaft controller 2003 with directory id MkWfVYpS_qAWFaz7GuOkRg

DRY RUN of removing KRaft controller 2003 with directory id MkWfVYpS_qAWFaz=
7GuOkRg

Cause:

The value supplied for %s already ends with a space, while the format strin=
g adds another space after %s:

System.out.printf("%s KRaft controller %d with directory id %s%n",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 dryRun ? "DRY RUN of removing " : "Removed ",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 controllerId,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 directoryId);

Suggested change:

System.out.printf("%sKRaft controller %d with directory id %s%n",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 dryRun ? "DRY RUN of removing " : "Removed ",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 controllerId,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 directoryId);

The corresponding unit-test expectation should also be changed to use one s=
pace.

This issue affects Apache Kafka 3.9.x through 4.3.x. It is already correcte=
d in 4.4.0 and trunk as part of KAFKA-20395 / PR #22191, but the correction=
 has not been backported to the affected release branches.

There is no functional impact; this only corrects the CLI output formatting=
.



