=EC=9D=B4=EC=84=A0=EB=AF=BC created KAFKA-21360:
---------------------------

             Summary: Heterogeneous simple share assignor keeps partitions =
of topics that no member subscribes to
                 Key: KAFKA-21360
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21360
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: group-coordinator
    Affects Versions: 4.2.0
            Reporter: =EC=9D=B4=EC=84=A0=EB=AF=BC
            Assignee: =EC=9D=B4=EC=84=A0=EB=AF=BC


union of the members' subscriptions. A topic that no member subscribes to a=
nymore is never visited, so a member whose existing assignment contains it =
gets its old partitions for that topic carried over into the new target ass=
ignment.

For the same reason, the {{else}} branch in {{TopicAssignmentPartialBuilder=
#revokeUnassignablePartitions}} that removes the topic is
unreachable, since {{topicId}} always comes from {{subscribedTopicIds}} the=
re.

The homogeneous builder handles this case correctly {{SimpleHomogeneousAssi=
gnmentBuilder}}
iterates over each member's existing assignment and removes topics that are=
 no longer subscribed.

This behavior has been present since the builder was introduced by KAFKA-19=
363
(https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/20074), and is present in 4.2.0.

h3. Reproduction

Invoke {{SimpleAssignor#assign}} with the following group specification:

* Topics: T1 (4 partitions), T2 (2 partitions), T3 (2 partitions)
* Member A subscribes to {T1}, existing assignment {T1=3D[0], T2=3D[0]}
* Member B subscribes to {T1, T3}, existing assignment {T1=3D[1], T2=3D[1]}
* Subscription type: HETEROGENEOUS

Actual assignor output (one observed run):
{noformat}
A=3D{T2=3D[0], T1=3D[0, 2]}
B=3D{T2=3D[1], T1=3D[1, 3], T3=3D[0, 1]}
{noformat}

Expected result: T2 is revoked from both members.

h3. Impact

Since KAFKA-19431, {{ShareGroupAssignmentBuilder}} filters out topics outsi=
de each member's subscription when reconciling the target assignment into t=
he member's current assignment, so these stale partitions are not passed on=
 to members.

This filtering does not modify the stored target assignment. The stale entr=
ies can therefore
survive subsequent rebalances while the group remains heterogeneous and no =
member subscribes to the topic.

This was found while adding tests in https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/2=
3874, where it was confirmed as a bug in review (https://github.com/apache/=
kafka/pull/23874#issuecomment-6394163465).



