Aditya Kousik created KAFKA-21361:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Distribution snapshots for Kafka client metrics
                 Key: KAFKA-21361
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21361
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: clients, metrics
            Reporter: Aditya Kousik
            Assignee: Aditya Kousik


Kafka clients report latency and size only as an average and a maximum over=
 the last 30 seconds. Both don't show how values are spread out during that=
 time. One slow request can pull the average far from a typical one, and=C2=
=A0there's no way to get a p50 or p99, or to combine numbers across clients=
 or over an hour.

We should propose a distribution API that lets clients count how many value=
s fall into each range, so metrics backends such as Prometheus and OpenTele=
metry can show real histograms and compute any percentile over any=C2=A0per=
iod.



--
