Hi all,

I'd like to start a discussion on KIP-1387, which adds a stat that counts la=
tency and size values into fixed bins and gives the bin counts to the metric=
s reporter.

KIP link: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/XwKDGw

Client latency and size metrics today are an average and a maximum over a 30=
-second window. We don=E2=80=99t get a view into how the values are spread, a=
 p99 can't be derived from them. A percentile computed inside the client can=
't be combined across clients or across windows whereas bin counts can. A re=
porter can publish them as a Prom or OTel histogram, and a backend query can=
 compute any percentile, over any period across the whole fleet.

The KIP adds DistributionStat, whose value is a DistributionSnapshot of cumu=
lative bin counts. Seven distributions are registered at INFO next to the ex=
isting -avg and -max metrics, with more at DEBUG. Existing metrics don't cha=
nge, and JmxReporter skips distributions, so a client reporting over JMX see=
s nothing new.

Looking forward to your feedback.

Thanks,=E2=80=A8Aditya



