Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21372) PartitionGroup#readyToProcess
 formats log messages on every call, and most of these messages are
 discarded
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Nicholas Telford (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Nicholas Telford created KAFKA-21372:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: PartitionGroup#readyToProcess formats log messages on=
 every call, and most of these messages are discarded
                 Key: KAFKA-21372
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21372
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 4.4.0, 4.3.0, 4.2.0
            Reporter: Nicholas Telford


h3. Problem

KAFKA-19682 (#20693, first released in 4.2.0) added a log message to {{{}Pa=
rtitionGroup#readyToProcess{}}}. The method returns this message in {{{}Rea=
dyToProcessResult{}}}. It builds the message with {{String.format}} and a {=
{StringBuilder}} for each partition that has no buffered records:
{code:java}
final Long fetchedLag =3D fetchedLags.getOrDefault(partition, -1L);
appendLog(logMessageBuilder, String.format("Partition %s has fetched lag of=
 %d", partition, fetchedLag));
...
appendLog(logMessageBuilder,
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 String.format("Partition %s has current lag %d, but no data i=
s buffered locally. Waiting to buffer some records.",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 partition, fetchedLag));
...
appendLog(logMessageBuilder, String.format(
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 "Partition %s has current lag 0 and current time is %d. " +
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 "Waiting for new data to be produced for config=
ured idle time %d (deadline is %d).",
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 partition, wallClockTime, maxTaskIdleMs, deadline));
{code}
No log-level check protects this code. It runs each time {{StreamTask#isPro=
cessable}} calls {{{}readyToProcess{}}}, and the {{TaskExecutor}} loop does=
 this {*}for each record{*}. The code runs when a task has more than one in=
put partition and at least one of those partitions has no buffered records.=
 This is a normal condition for a task that reads a low-volume topic togeth=
er with a high-volume topic.

The caller then discards almost every message:
 * {{StreamTask#isProcessable}} discards the message when the task changes =
from READY to NOT_READY ({{{}wasReady{}}}).
 * {{StreamTask#maybeLogNotReady}} logs the message at INFO only when {{NOT=
_READY_LOG_INTERVAL_MS}} (120 s) passed since the last log. It discards all=
 other messages.
 * When a partition reaches its idle deadline and the task becomes ready ({=
{{}enforced{}}}), the method returns {{{}ReadyToProcessResult(true, Optiona=
l.empty()){}}}. It discards the "has fetched lag" text that it already form=
atted for that partition.

Before 4.2.0, this method logged the same states with {{{}logger.trace("...=
{}...", ...){}}}. That code formatted no text when TRACE was disabled.
h3. Impact

We upgraded a Kafka Streams application from 3.8 to 4.4.0. The application =
runs EOS v2 and has several sub-topologies with more than one input partiti=
on for each task.

We recorded a 5-minute JFR profile on one instance during the catch-up afte=
r a restart. In this profile:
 * {{PartitionGroup#readyToProcess}} is 19.7% of the StreamThread CPU sampl=
es. {{String.format}} called from it is 15.1%, and this includes {{DecimalF=
ormatSymbols.<init>}} and {{{}Formatter.parse{}}}.
 * {{ArrayList}} allocations from {{Formatter.parse}} are 13.7% of the samp=
led allocation weight.

The 3.8 profile of the same application has no equivalent cost.
h3. Proposed fix

Do not build the message unless the caller will log it. Possible approaches=
:
 # Return the not-ready reason as structured data in {{{}ReadyToProcessResu=
lt{}}}: the partition, the fetched lag, the deadline and the reason. Let {{=
StreamTask#maybeLogNotReady}} format the text only when it logs.
 # Alternatively, make {{readyToProcess}} build the message only when the c=
aller asks for it. For example, pass a flag that {{StreamTask}} sets when {=
{NOT_READY_LOG_INTERVAL_MS}} passed.

Both approaches keep the log output of KAFKA-19682 and remove the cost from=
 the processing loop.
h3. Workaround

{{max.task.idle.ms=3D-1}} makes {{readyToProcess}} return before the loop. =
But this setting also disables the wait for unfetched data, so a task can p=
rocess records out of order. It is not a safe workaround for applications t=
hat need the default behaviour.



--
