Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-21380) Failed state-transition rollback
 bypasses DLQ when delivery count limit is reached
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "da Yi (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

da Yi created KAFKA-21380:
-----------------------------

             Summary: Failed state-transition rollback bypasses DLQ when de=
livery count limit is reached
                 Key: KAFKA-21380
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-21380
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: consumer
    Affects Versions: 4.5.0
            Reporter: da Yi
            Assignee: da Yi


When the DLQ flow is enabled for a share group (KIP-1191), records whose de=
livery
count reaches the limit are moved to ARCHIVING on the normal release path s=
o they
are written to the DLQ topic (InFlightState.tryUpdateState with dlqSupportE=
nabled=3Dtrue).

However, the rollback path in InFlightState.completeStateTransition(false) =
- taken
when a two-phase state transition fails (e.g. the persister write fails) an=
d the
acquisition lock has expired - archives the records directly:

=C2=A0 =C2=A0 state =3D previousState.deliveryCount() >=3D rollbackState.ma=
xDeliveryCount ?
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 RecordState.ARCHIVED : RecordState.AVAILABLE;

This bypasses the DLQ flow entirely: records that should have been dead-let=
tered are
silently archived and never appear in the DLQ topic. Two related inconsiste=
ncies:
1. ARCHIVING (normal path) vs ARCHIVED (rollback path) for the same limit-r=
eached
=C2=A0 =C2=A0condition.
2. The normal path evaluates the limit with the delivery count including th=
e current
=C2=A0 =C2=A0delivery, while the rollback path uses previousState.deliveryC=
ount() - the counts
=C2=A0 =C2=A0differ by one.

Note that completeStateTransition(boolean) has no access to the dlqSupportE=
nabled
flag, so the rollback path cannot currently reach ARCHIVING.

Reproduction: new unit test InFlightStateTest
(testFailedStateTransitionWithExpiredLockDeadLettersWhenDlqSupported) fails=
 on
trunk and passes with the fix.

Proposed fix: thread the DLQ-support flag through the rollback path, mirror=
ing the
normal transition path, and start the DLQ flow for batches that move to ARC=
HIVING
in both the local rollback and the persister-failure paths.

Two test scenarios (step 5 in the reproduction) verify:
- normal release path at the limit moves records to ARCHIVING (baseline)
- rollback with expired lock at the limit moves records to ARCHIVING when D=
LQ is
=C2=A0 enabled, and to ARCHIVED when disabled



--
