t
> changes, using a content token echoed by the client. Clients log the valu=
es on
> first receipt and on change, and warn when a stored override differs from=
 the
> value in effect. Client behavior does not change.
>
> On the release: KIP-1313 introduces a new version of every RPC in 4.5. If=
 this
> KIP lands in the same release, I would like to add the fields to those
> versions in coordination with KAFKA-20925. Andrew, I would appreciate you=
r view
> on whether that works.
